  "interpretation": [
    "Across complete TT, SS and FF 16-pair matrices, 5 ps-to-1 ps PCLK source energy differences are larger than timing and terminal-magnitude deltas; the largest absolute PEX delta is 0.5021 fJ (FF 01-to-00), and the largest relative PEX delta is 15.83% (SS 01-to-00).",
    "The selected 0.5 ps reruns include each profile/stage maximum or a worst-case companion from the 5 ps-to-1 ps comparison. All targeted baseline and PEX cases passed, with no contract failures or ngspice Error lines.",
    "Among the selected refinements, the maximum 1 ps-to-0.5 ps energy change is below 0.89% for the schematic baseline and below 0.51% for PEX. This supports using the 1 ps value as the reference for the recorded setup; it is a targeted convergence check, not a full 0.5 ps matrix.",
    "Energy is net energy delivered by an ideal VPCLK source over one cycle window, including returned energy. It is not dissipation of a physical PCLK source/driver. The model uses schematic WL buffers and estimated 17.4 fF row loads."
  ],
